#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133895 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133711 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/id #uuid "a817c3c6-97bb-55e4-9a1e-04ed99d3eaab" :question/math-academy-id "e-9553" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\oint\\limits_C \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in $\\mathbb{R}^2,$ which of the following could be the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\left\\langle -y, \\: y\\right\\rangle$\n\nII. $\\left\\langle -2x, \\: 2x\\right\\rangle$\n\nIII. $\\left\\langle 5y\\sin x, \\: x-5\\cos x \\right\\rangle$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $\\mathbf{F}(x,y) = \\left\\langle P(x,y), \\: Q(x,y) \\right\\rangle,$ where\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I gives the required area. In this case, \n$\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = -1$\nand\n$\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} = 0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II does not give the required area. In this case, \n$\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 0$\nand\n$\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} = 2,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 2.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 5\\sin x$\nand\n$\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} = 1+5\\sin x,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051070}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134092 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe357184-c804-53e5-9673-6bcefc79fd9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439453} {:answer/id #uuid "0918b264-4f40-5876-987b-5c8750a26cc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe357184-c804-53e5-9673-6bcefc79fd9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439453} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3372797-44ff-5f24-b147-8ec1e085072b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440084} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0842fe57-c4b3-512a-a06a-8b846341aac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439455} {:answer/id #uuid "586a0c72-4a76-59c2-8374-26e889f264c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0842fe57-c4b3-512a-a06a-8b846341aac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439455} :answer-field/id #uuid "d69bbf46-abac-5660-b279-f3c0fe70f969" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440085} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85cdaefa-89de-57a1-b19f-0c380903a4f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439457} {:answer/id #uuid "0d933456-9721-5edd-b8fc-3dc9d94ba641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d933456-9721-5edd-b8fc-3dc9d94ba641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439458} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac6e472f-13b9-5a6e-8237-3f44c55c1cc5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d72f3f4-6ff1-53f9-94a6-72b405d3f343" :question/math-academy-id "q-125852" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the functions $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P(x,y)=y$ and $Q(x,y)=-x$\n- **II.** $P(x,y)=\\frac{x}{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)=\\frac{y}{2}$\n- **III.** $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Pair I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134093 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2b8c17c-21b8-507b-8420-d670c4b65f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439459} {:answer/id #uuid "17e98f8a-da18-55f0-8939-1564456b888b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2b8c17c-21b8-507b-8420-d670c4b65f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439459} :answer-field/id #uuid "182f9891-f2da-5a34-881d-2dc0e9bd1216" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440087} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aff01827-2164-503c-885f-729ce07f69b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439461} {:answer/id #uuid "41f3acaf-c391-5b28-bea3-53dc115237b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41f3acaf-c391-5b28-bea3-53dc115237b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439462} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6bbea9d-55dc-56d4-af3c-6bb5a3355e6e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440088} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c35b0a14-7ff3-5770-b606-c1b4ba2b788d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439463} {:answer/id #uuid "c0470289-cbe4-59c9-abaf-f84a85ae4c3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0470289-cbe4-59c9-abaf-f84a85ae4c3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439464} :answer-field/id #uuid "f690e279-0ebb-573a-bc24-60532b449e8c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0916e138-1ac3-5dc1-b5d3-86d819d37c90" :question/math-academy-id "q-125853" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,{x}^{2}+x⟩$\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{4}+x,\\,\\frac{3x}{4}⟩$\n- **III.** $F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,0⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x+1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2x+2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{4}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{3}{4},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369359 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ae6522b-d021-5d59-8cd6-f5304bdd55ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437758} {:answer/id #uuid "a8414dbe-30d0-5384-b8c5-62cc6232e458" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8414dbe-30d0-5384-b8c5-62cc6232e458" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437759} :answer-field/id #uuid "748fe4bc-f5a7-5f6e-a198-2ec4af1a9fb6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5fcddd5-827b-5326-b25a-877e35a9d273" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437760} {:answer/id #uuid "1f174d76-4611-5f5a-bb29-5066e184e17e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5fcddd5-827b-5326-b25a-877e35a9d273" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437760} :answer-field/id #uuid "93da9704-e1a5-5081-8553-7cd992df06d2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438909} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cffa29f7-20b1-5b11-99da-52f6143261ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437762} {:answer/id #uuid "c4926ca4-8616-57f1-a942-8235f95a7902" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4926ca4-8616-57f1-a942-8235f95a7902" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437763} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3c21734-8e5a-535d-ada3-66000108f100" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf5aefc1-27f1-5c4b-be31-6e2e9699a7da" :question/math-academy-id "q-126560" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the functions $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P(x,y)={e}^{x+y}-\\frac{y}{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={e}^{x+y}+\\frac{x}{2}$\n- **II.** $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- **III.** $P(x,y)=x$ and $Q(x,y)=x$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Pair I gives the required area.  In this case,\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{x+y}-\\frac{1}{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{x+y}+\\frac{1}{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area.  Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369366 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95f3c085-feb8-513f-add4-66aa98bd17ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437764} {:answer/id #uuid "5fe0d2ca-9939-5556-96db-9df34ee271ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fe0d2ca-9939-5556-96db-9df34ee271ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437765} :answer-field/id #uuid "18de6163-4953-583e-b212-b0337c772ec5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dc332b0-9c6c-52fb-9960-0a34a7b12892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437766} {:answer/id #uuid "218378a4-fbcd-5e98-8eff-a70c74b13433" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dc332b0-9c6c-52fb-9960-0a34a7b12892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437766} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d6dd72a-3e01-555e-a264-373480cb3397" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438912} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8116a580-f40c-5f87-8318-cb566921d6e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437768} {:answer/id #uuid "ebb283d0-c938-5e90-8f21-2d9015525c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebb283d0-c938-5e90-8f21-2d9015525c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437769} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1cf9841-fb2d-5f21-9260-8a5cc7b8a700" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5decc408-adb2-55a3-accb-8195735690a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-126571" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F(x,y)=⟨0,\\,x⟩$\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{y},\\,y⟩$\n- **III.** $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{5}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,\\,\\frac{4x}{5}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{y}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{e}^{y}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{5}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4}{5},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5314efe-6d3d-5874-a4e8-e3bb02359b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437782} {:answer/id #uuid "de7792c1-6264-5b26-a11b-f266fd2ffbf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5314efe-6d3d-5874-a4e8-e3bb02359b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437782} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d9aea2b-8ded-5e68-bdc8-80f01907fab2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f3e2c30-0387-56e6-9017-184fe08df055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437784} {:answer/id #uuid "cca9abd2-28b1-50b1-a0d7-213e565a3526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f3e2c30-0387-56e6-9017-184fe08df055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437784} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cf91cf4-1adf-55a1-bef6-7fd579465082" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438921} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e066b5f-ee40-571e-9d64-c19fe307ffad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437786} {:answer/id #uuid "5cbbfdda-889f-50b7-8d61-3c68b8acb082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cbbfdda-889f-50b7-8d61-3c68b8acb082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437787} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dea6355-4414-5031-bdce-266f0e70af29" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a19e15dc-6544-52f9-9d54-2c5e5b2885d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-126577" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F(x,y)=⟨y,\\,y⟩$\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=⟨\\frac{y}{7},\\,\\frac{6x}{7}⟩$\n- **III.** $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{x}-{e}^{-y},\\,x{e}^{-y}+x⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II does *not* give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{7}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{6}{7},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{5}{7}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area.  Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{-y}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{-y}+1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7834049-c71e-58d4-8d98-c09398226feb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437770} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e567b4-b8c2-531b-be4a-6a987225a67c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7834049-c71e-58d4-8d98-c09398226feb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437770} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e6cf9cf-573c-532b-8b70-05635308acab" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438914} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d458576b-4e27-54ad-b0dd-01c8de1730f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437772} {:answer/id #uuid "95452bb7-2fca-5e83-88ee-5eea11dc8b4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d458576b-4e27-54ad-b0dd-01c8de1730f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437772} :answer-field/id #uuid "15e08b68-718b-5246-ad09-cfa2adcaab8c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438915} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "937e30c9-442f-5622-a5d1-c5a8f129c9c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437774} {:answer/id #uuid "8e713a4f-cc2e-59f3-b27f-a7992c92588d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e713a4f-cc2e-59f3-b27f-a7992c92588d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437775} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3f9770d-2312-582c-8540-7d2ef01450c3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d67db6a-7337-599e-8ecc-26284642ae3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-126574" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F(x,y)=⟨y{e}^{x},\\,x-{e}^{x}⟩$\n\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=⟨2y,\\,x⟩$\n\n- **III.** $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{2x}{3}+1⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{x}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1-{e}^{x},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-2{e}^{x}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II does *not* give the required area. Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{3}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{2}{3},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21740e2f-600c-5a93-859b-56d238cd0e09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437776} {:answer/id #uuid "2b9be679-baf3-5630-ae88-5b57cb494970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21740e2f-600c-5a93-859b-56d238cd0e09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437776} :answer-field/id #uuid "b64b88b3-d28a-5b4a-a38b-7fe8543c12b6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438917} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11bfb2c2-cc66-55c8-bec6-1505afc317a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437778} {:answer/id #uuid "8905b533-fda6-553c-b3a2-e716938166b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8905b533-fda6-553c-b3a2-e716938166b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437779} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfac5d71-e652-5d4b-8ce8-de5480e6fd0d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438918} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f5c9797-7316-5214-93dc-7545c27a4470" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437780} {:answer/id #uuid "c013a325-7790-52f3-85d6-c6452b7b6dab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c013a325-7790-52f3-85d6-c6452b7b6dab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437781} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebf7a35d-36f8-551d-abfc-0f58ffd44dd7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c0dea55-217c-592d-9a6c-d305c8e67729" :question/math-academy-id "q-126575" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F(x,y)=⟨{y}^{3},\\,{x}^{3}+1⟩$\n\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=⟨\\frac{y}{2}+\\sqrt{2}x,\\,\\frac{3x}{2}⟩$\n\n- **III.** $F(x,y)=⟨x,\\,x⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3{y}^{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=3{x}^{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{3}{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02757ddb-6720-5404-868b-7b1166fb2c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510781} {:answer/id #uuid "083e8245-b859-5f0f-b493-6e1eb22d754b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510797} {:answer/id #uuid "1e791730-85c4-5ff7-ad54-6e399657153c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510851} {:answer/id #uuid "3c70ca77-ec27-57f8-b078-51030fa03414" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510920} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d4bd2c-dd7d-5ebf-8ab9-0d013cef2b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2d4bd2c-dd7d-5ebf-8ab9-0d013cef2b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511284} :answer-field/id #uuid "1557ad1a-a45b-592a-8609-24271802b200" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ae04e3b-017d-534f-b76c-ac600584e435" :question/math-academy-id "q-126568" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the functions $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)?$\n\nI. $P(x,y)=-y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$\n\nII. $P(x,y)=x$ and $Q(x,y)=y$\n\nIII. $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=6{y}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Pair I gives the required area. In this case,\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cd6483d-ff42-5dc9-bf60-d49b491388dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560464} {:answer/id #uuid "5000cc2e-e84a-572e-94b0-98de14def1b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560539} {:answer/id #uuid "683ef1d0-3a45-5daf-a0c7-cf2a0f6be250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560583} {:answer/id #uuid "be4e7b49-1ac4-5e2f-92d1-d5c217fc797f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560741} {:answer/id #uuid "dd5e01ff-4835-5778-92d5-2ea89a8203bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cd6483d-ff42-5dc9-bf60-d49b491388dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560464} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea3760f2-d10c-5617-a3f3-b8335b0f89d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d6a46ea-e810-5ed6-9d15-12e3845c1e76" :question/math-academy-id "q-126572" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nI. $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{y}-y,\\,x{e}^{y}⟩$\n\nII. $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{y},\\,0⟩$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{5}+{x}^{7},\\,\\frac{6x}{5}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I give the required area. In this case,\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{y}-1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{y},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II does *not* give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{e}^{y}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{y}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III does *not* give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{5}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{6}{5},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{7}{5}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561018 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18fdc301-b9e6-5380-b576-f756ad837d6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560422} {:answer/id #uuid "48d9075b-21bf-518c-85e4-b52a39ca48c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560525} {:answer/id #uuid "71000db5-1bfa-5f19-88d0-bfac331f25f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560605} {:answer/id #uuid "79fb9fa0-3c09-5639-8f51-38fc29793534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560625} {:answer/id #uuid "aee8fb2f-93bf-5e56-b3ef-5f91d5ed3421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48d9075b-21bf-518c-85e4-b52a39ca48c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560525} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b9b5f42-303d-5796-888d-e11c20c8cac2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7d76f5fb-ba28-5b32-904d-cbb78731c152" :question/math-academy-id "q-126570" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the functions $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)?$\n\nI. $P(x,y)=-\\frac{y}{3}$ and $Q(x,y)=\\frac{x}{3}$\n\nII. $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $Q(x,y)=x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n\nIII. $P(x,y)={y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Pair I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{3}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{3},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{2}{3}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III does *not* give the required area. Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2y$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2x-2y\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5caa2745-f258-5524-bce2-0cee34f7a871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560562} {:answer/id #uuid "7484861d-d825-59f3-b995-2fbd5e8a6934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560612} {:answer/id #uuid "81e94b1a-bd75-573d-86e7-53f24a85af34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560639} {:answer/id #uuid "8ccdd078-e1bf-5bbc-be52-fd411e22349d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560656} {:answer/id #uuid "fbcde265-3bb2-5d78-a137-ab8cf1e73dcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ccdd078-e1bf-5bbc-be52-fd411e22349d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560656} :answer-field/id #uuid "041132e8-077c-5837-a79f-29852017427b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f61d70b2-c968-54d9-b087-2ae80ef01b89" :question/math-academy-id "q-126561" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the functions $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)?$\n\nI. $P(x,y)={e}^{y}$ and $Q(x,y)={e}^{x}$\n\nII. $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=y$\n\nIII. $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=y$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Pair I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{y}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{x},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{x}-{e}^{y}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area.  Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "536431fa-077c-5c63-8e52-e720d5f25ad5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560546} {:answer/id #uuid "57095cd5-869a-52ea-98e5-ae49745a6cf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560553} {:answer/id #uuid "58122a63-9d7f-591f-b933-aa93158e184f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560555} {:answer/id #uuid "629d2292-4c54-5f88-aab2-977463ff11a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560573} {:answer/id #uuid "88b89e38-2d3c-57a2-ad5a-0be2309918a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "629d2292-4c54-5f88-aab2-977463ff11a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560573} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bca7dbd-ffdc-5cb7-822a-009c4eccd416" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f892a9d1-561b-51b8-a283-3b892f8dc787" :question/math-academy-id "q-126559" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the functions $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)?$\n\nI. $P(x,y)=y$ and $Q(x,y)=x$\n\nII. $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0$\n\nIII. $P(x,y)=y+{e}^{x}$ and $Q(x,y)=\\frac{y}{3}$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Pair I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III does *not* give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}]}
